PRE-TABLE AMENDMENT, PASS 11 BATCH TWO -- its own file (mtime against part12/driver.log is the order witness).

SECTION 20 -- the ENUMERATION across the arms, and the TxCTL generating set it demands.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHY A SECOND BATCH: three consecutive passes found ONE class -- an unvaried axis crossed with a varied
  one (190 -> 194 -> 203 -> 218) -- and the class-closure amendment says the next repair owes THE
  ENUMERATION across the arms, not another cell (the pass-11 Opus seat said the same and derived, not
  measured, that at TxCTL two of the {COVF} x {idata & ~7} cells are unheld).
* THE ENUMERATION (now in the contract): nine arms have bodies with no `if' on state or idata -- the plain
  rows hold them; IPL has one static latch, held both ways; TxICR is closed by passes 9-11; TxCTL has the
  label as an RMW index, the count class, and two tested idata bits (COVF, `~7') with COVF-set held at NO
  cell and the HUH? bits held only at the plain cell (0xaab8).
* THE GENERATING SET AT TxCTL: in the four overflow sessions (count 1, count >= 8, each timer) write
  0x0004 (COVF) and 0x0008 (a HUH? bit) at the armed label, then preset the idle label's CTL to 0x02 (COC
  without CEN -- CEN would start the idle timer) and write 0x0000 / 0x0004 / 0x0008 there; a `huh' row
  per session counts the TxCTL HUH? print.  Twenty-four rows -> 242.  Appended, so the existing indices
  do not move.
* LANDED VALUES (the preset-collision check): count 1 (0x11): 0x0004 -> (0x11 & 0xfc) | 0 = 0x10, COVF
  clears OVF|COVF -> 0x00; 0x0008 -> 0x10 + HUH?.  Count >= 8 (0x81): 0x0004 -> 0x00; 0x0008 -> 0x80
  (masked 0x80 != 0x81) + HUH?.  Idle preset 0x02: any landed write -> 0x00.  None equals a preset.
* ALSO IN THIS BATCH (Opus, pass 11): cval()'s value branch on a LIVE guest with a short transcript now says
  "short-transcript (FAILED FOR SOME OTHER REASON)" instead of a bare "died"; the (T1, 0, 0, IEN clear)
  cell is attributed to `op t1icr dcl' (0x0303), not to `latch all', which never writes T1ICR.
* THE FOUR MANDATED CHECKS:
  - SIBLING PARITY -- every new write is made at BOTH labels in every overflow session (the armed label
    and the idle one); the guest path stays T2-only by construction, disclosed as before.
  - CLAIM -> ROW -- "COVF-set held at every count cell" -> the `*v' readbacks; "the HUH? bits held at
    every count cell" -> the `*x' readbacks and the `huh' rows; "the idle label of each count cell held"
    -> the `rb1' / `rb2' readbacks; "COVF at the 0xfc and plain cells not written" -> disclosed with the
    reason (a filed path; a preset that would start the timer).
  - GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- unchanged: the guard cannot see the count, the label or the idata bits;
    the readbacks and the HUH? print are the channel.
  - CHANNEL -- ovf*/ovfhi* rbv <- M_COVF and M_COVFOVF (0x00 vs 0x11 / 0x81); rb1v / rb2v <- M_COVF
    (0x00 vs 0x02); rbx <- M_TXHIOVF (0x10 / 0x80) with huh <- M_TXHIOVF (1 vs 0); rb1 / rb2 <- no
    mutant in this table (the idle-label 0x0000 cell with the other timer's count held; the same shape as
    M_P2T1 at TxICR, killed there); rb1x / rb2x <- no mutant in this table (the idle label's HUH? bit:
    `&& !((idata & ~7) && !(reg & OVF))' would red them).  Stated, not hidden.
* THE ORDER MATTERS UNDER A MUTANT: a landed COVF write clears the count, so an OVF-conditioned guard
  RE-ARMS for the later writes in the session; the predictions derive the readbacks in session order.
* HAND-VERIFIED before writing on the restored part-10b clone (p13_try.py) -- see the note appended below
  by the verification step, or the absence of one.
